msgctxt "80"
msgid "I'm going back to Morning Glory."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "92"
msgid ""
"Understood. But what about Mine? It's entirely possible he's\r\n"
"already en route to Kamurocho to get rid of Daigo once and\r\n"
"for all."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "104"
msgid "I need to take care of my kids, Joji. That's the first priority."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "116"
msgid ""
"...Right. At the very least, I may have a way to get you to\r\n"
"Tokyo quicker once you're done."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "128"
msgid "What do you mean?"
msgstr "Cosa intendi?"

msgctxt "140"
msgid ""
"I'll reach out to CIA headquarters, see if I can arrange something over at "
"one of the military bases. I'll need to head up to Tokyo myself soon enough,"
" after all."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "152"
msgid ""
"Oh, and there's no question that Mine is working with Black Monday. Meaning "
"he'll more likely than not be waiting for you at the hospital."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "164"
msgid "I imagine Richardson will be there, too."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "176"
msgid ""
"That's the leader of Black Monday, right? I remember Tamiya\r\n"
"telling me about him."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "188"
msgid ""
"Yes. Unfortunately even with the CIA's massive information\r\n"
"network, all we have is his name. The man is an enigma."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "200"
msgid ""
"One thing is for sure, though. He's responsible for every\r\n"
"last operation Black Monday has ever put into motion."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "212"
msgid ""
"If Tamiya told you about Richardson, I assume you were also\r\n"
"told about our plan to lure him out. Assuming it's worked,\r\n"
"I'll need to go to Tokyo to finally arrest him."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "224"
msgid ""
"In other words, leave the transportation to me. You get home\r\n"
"to your kids."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "236"
msgid "Thanks, Joji. I appreciate it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "248"
msgid "Let's go, Taichi."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "260"
msgid "We gotta hurry!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "284"
msgid "Are you sure you can just let Toma go like this?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "296"
msgid "What do you mean? You're the one who asked me to do it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "308"
msgid ""
"Well, from the way Tamiya put it, it sounded like CIA orders\r\n"
"were absolute for you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "320"
msgid ""
"Is me beating you in a fight really all it takes for you to\r\n"
"abandon that resolve?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "332"
msgid ""
"Hmph, I see what you're getting at. I can't deny the importance of the CIA "
"in my life, but I work by my own methods. All they care about is achieving "
"the proper result."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "344"
msgid ""
"Meaning Daigo and Nakahara were shot in order to achieve\r\n"
"that \"result\"?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "356"
msgid "Well..."
msgstr "Beh..."

msgctxt "368"
msgid "I still don't believe you'd do that, even if you'd been ordered to."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "380"
msgid "......"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "392"
msgid "So tell me the truth, Joji. Was it really you who shot them?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "404"
msgid "...I suppose I do owe you an explanation."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "416"
msgid "I'm all ears."
msgstr "Sono tutt'orecchi."

msgctxt "428"
msgid ""
"The truth of it is, what happened to Shigeru Nakahara and Daigo Dojima was "
"an unfortunate side effect of our concerted efforts to pass the military "
"expansion bill."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "440"
msgid ""
"But there would have been no need to shoot them under normal circumstances."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "452"
msgid "What!?"
msgstr "Cosa!?"

msgctxt "464"
msgid "The one responsible for that was a colleague of mine."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "476"
msgid "Another CIA agent?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "488"
msgid ""
"Yes. In Nakahara's case, we were trying to obtain the deed to his land. But "
"what happened to Daigo Dojima was all an unfortunate misunderstanding."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "500"
msgid "What do you mean, a misunderstanding?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "512"
msgid ""
"Daigo panicked when he saw me put my hand in my pocket.\r\n"
"Yakuza instinct, I suppose."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "524"
msgid ""
"He must have thought I was going for my gun, then before I\r\n"
"knew it he had his own weapon trained on me."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "536"
msgid "So your friend shot him."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "548"
msgid ""
"Correct. It wasn't dissimilar to how things went down with Nakahara. The "
"first thing he did when we barged in demanding the deed was go for his gun."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "560"
msgid ""
"And this other agent... Is he one of the foreigners I ran\r\n"
"into in Kamurocho?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "572"
msgid ""
"Yes. I must make it clear, we try our best to avoid taking\r\n"
"lives in our line of work, even when the mission is at risk.\r\n"
"But under those circumstances, we simply had no choice."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "584"
msgid "No choice, huh...?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "596"
msgid ""
"Even still, I would be lying if I said I didn't feel pangs\r\n"
"of guilt over what happened."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "608"
msgid "Don't. You're not the one who shot them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "620"
msgid ""
"True, but the only reason we've arrived at this point is the agenda put "
"forth by the CIA."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "632"
msgid ""
"The least I can do now is offer an apology. If possible, I'd\r\n"
"like to do the same to both of the men impacted by all this."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "644"
msgid ""
"You can apologize to Nakahara right now. He's already out of\r\n"
"the hospital."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "656"
msgid ""
"I'm glad to hear that, but I don't have the authority to talk to a civilian "
"about these matters."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "668"
msgid "Everything we're doing here is highly confidential, after all."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "680"
msgid ""
"That explains why you can't tell him anything, but the CIA won't even let "
"you meet with him? That seems... strict."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "692"
msgid ""
"Strict as it may be, that's the way it is. I've killed far more than my fair"
" share of men in this line of duty."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "704"
msgid ""
"But atoning for those lives that I've taken... is impossible.\r\n"
"Going against a direct CIA mandate. That impossibility is\r\n"
"the most difficult part of this job."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "716"
msgid ""
"I'll tell Nakahara myself, then. That wouldn't be a problem,\r\n"
"would it?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "728"
msgid ""
"No, please do. And please apologize to Daigo as well once\r\n"
"you're back in Tokyo."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "740"
msgid "Daigo? Do you know where he is?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "752"
msgid "You don't?"
msgstr "Ah, no?"

msgctxt "764"
msgid ""
"No. Kashiwagi-san told me he couldn't risk letting that information out in "
"case it fell into the wrong hands."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "776"
msgid "So then nobody else knows where he is?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "788"
msgid "As far as I know."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "800"
msgid "I need more certainty than that, Kiryu."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "812"
msgid ""
"All I know is what Kashiwagi-san told me. What difference\r\n"
"would it make, anyway?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "824"
msgid ""
"Let me ask you something. What do you think Mine would do\r\n"
"if he found out Daigo was still alive?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "836"
msgid "Mine? What does he have to do with this?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "848"
msgid ""
"Daigo is nothing more than an obstacle on his path toward\r\n"
"Tojo Clan chairmanship, yes? He wouldn't just stand by and\r\n"
"watch if he knew Daigo hadn't been killed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "860"
msgid "Are you saying Mine knows where Daigo is?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "872"
msgid ""
"It's difficult to know either way. But I can't rule out the possibility."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "884"
msgid ""
"And if Mine is working with Black Monday, he'll have total\r\n"
"access to their information network."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "896"
msgid ""
"In other words... As long as there's a chance Mine knows\r\n"
"where he is, Daigo is in grave danger."
msgstr ""

